          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{H}
            %em vacuum energy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+determinant"} functional determinant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} det_{reg}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi log
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z \coloneqq -log\,det_{reg} H
                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#InTermsOfSpecialValuesOfZetaFunctions In terms of special values of the zeta function
          %p
            The vacuum energy is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+values+of+L-functions"} special value
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+of+an+elliptic+differential+operator"} zeta function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_H
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            at 0:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z = -\frac{1}{2}\zeta_H^\prime(0)
                  \\,.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "zeta+function+of+an+elliptic+differential+operator#FunctionalDeterminant"} zeta function of an elliptic differential operator – Functional determinant
            for more.
          %h3#in_terms_of_the_path_integral_and_relation_to_generating_function In terms of the path integral and relation to generating function
          %p
            Traditionally the vacuum energy is expressed in terms of a hypothetical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            %a{:href => "#InTermsOfSpecialValuesOfZetaFunctions"} above
            zeta-function formalization this is not rigorous, but it serves to give the idea of
            %em why
            this is the vacuum energy and the the zeta-function expression may be taken to be the rigorous definition of the path integral heuristics.)
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogy
            with finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gaussian+integrals"} Gaussian integrals
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Feynman+diagram#ForFinitelyManyDegreesOfFreedom"} Feynman diagram – For finitely many degrees of freedom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+amplitude"} vacuum amplitude
            version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            (no
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            insertions, no
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary conditions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi D
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\phi \in \mathbf{Fields}}{\int}
                  \\exp(- S_H(\phi))
                  D\phi
                  \=
                  (det_reg H)^{-1/2}
                  \\,.
          %p Therefore
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %munder
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi D
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mi log
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  log
                  \\underset{\phi \in \mathbf{Fields}}{\int}
                  \\exp(- S_H(\phi))
                  D\phi
                  \=
                  \-\frac{1}{2}log\, det_{reg} H
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generating+functional"} generating functional
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+functions"} n-point functions
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Scrucca"}> Scrucca, section 1.6
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Edelstein13"} Edelstein 13, page 2
          %h3#as_holomorphic_potential_for_determinant_line_bundle As holomorphic potential for Determinant line bundle
          %p Regard
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ≔
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h \coloneqq \frac{1}{2} det_{reg}H
          %p
            as a hermitian structure on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
            = succeed "-squared" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
            with respect to a local trivializing section (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+connection"} Chern connection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h|_{U_i} = {\Vert \phi_i \Vert}^2
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then this line bundle is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen85"} Quillen 85
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Freed87"} Freed 87, p. 18
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Qiu12"} Qiu 12, section 2.8.1
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+connection"} Chern connection
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi log
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A = \partial log(h) = \partial \frac{1}{2} det_{reg}H = \partial Z
          %p
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-form"} differential 2-form
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                  %mover
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Z
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F = i \bar \partial\partial Z
                  \\,.
          %blockquote
            %p
              eh? Something wrong with the factors of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2
              here…
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#the_solution_to_the_strong_cp_problem_via_axions The solution to the strong CP problem via axions
          %p
            In the solution to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+CP+problem"} strong CP problem
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axions"} axions
            it is analysis of the dependency of the vacuum energy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            on the
            %span.newWikiWord
              theta-angle
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/theta-angle"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            which is argued to show that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axion"} axion
            expectation value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta = \langle a \rangle
            vanishes (
            %a{:href => "#VafaWitten84"}> Vafa-Witten 84
            ).
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "axion#AsASolutionToTheStrongCPProblem"} axion – As a solution to the strong CP-problem
